+## 1. Evidence-first reranker rubric
+
+- [ ] 1.1 Update the versioned Russian reranker system prompt with the ordered evidence-first comparison procedure: identify explicit tender requirements, compare them against supplied candidate evidence, reject direct contradictions, and use retrieval ranks only as secondary signals; verify the prompt still requires JSON-only output and preserves the compatible-candidate-over-`NOT_FOUND` principle.
+- [ ] 1.2 Add the bounded ball-valve passage/execution guidance for explicit full, reduced, and standard terminology, including that a stated conflicting passage type is not preferable merely because it is specialized or highly ranked; verify generic ball-valve requests do not gain an inferred passage requirement by prompt-contract tests.
+
+## 2. Focused regression coverage
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Add focused tests that load the versioned prompt and assert the required evidence ordering, missing-evidence treatment, explicit passage/execution distinction, contradiction handling, JSON contract, and existing `NOT_FOUND` rule are present without asserting any benchmark query, catalog ID, or GOLD result.
+- [ ] 2.2 Extend mocked reranker tests to verify the unchanged model request configuration and selected candidate-id ordering remain intact after the prompt update; verify response parsing still handles `MATCHED` and `NOT_FOUND` under the existing contract.
+
+## 3. Verification
+
+- [ ] 3.1 Run the focused reranker and matcher tests, then run `python -m pytest -q`; resolve product-code or test failures without adding candidate filtering, a second model call, harness-label imports, catalog-ID mappings, or retrieval/index changes.

